sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Steward
    participant Page as SIR page<br/>PdfExportModal
    participant Api as API routes<br/>/api/pdf
    participant Job as Background job<br/>processPdfJob
    participant DB as Supabase DB
    participant S3 as AWS S3

    Note over Steward,S3: Covers US 7.0.1. The PDF job flow exists for Admins.<br/>"(proposed)" = the step is not in the code today.

    Steward->>Page: Select Export PDF on own SIR (proposed for stewards)
    Page->>Api: POST /api/pdf {mode single, responseId,<br/>includeImages true}
    Api->>DB: getResponseOwnerId(responseId) (proposed)
    DB-->>Api: Owner user_id
    Api->>Api: Allow owner or Admin (proposed)<br/>Today: only role admin from user_metadata
    alt Caller did not submit the SIR (AT 2)
        Api-->>Page: 403. No job is made
        Page-->>Steward: Show "not allowed"
    else Caller owns the SIR
        Api->>DB: Insert S26_pdf_jobs row, status pending
        Api-->>Page: 202 with jobId
        Api->>Job: after(): processPdfJob(jobId)
        Job->>DB: fetchReportData: answers and attachments
        Job->>S3: Get photos with presigned GET
        Job->>Job: Render PDF (lib/pdf/inspectionReport)
        alt Render or upload fails
            Job->>DB: Set job failed with error
            Page-->>Steward: PdfExportsDropdown shows Failed
        else PDF is made
            Job->>S3: Put PDF
            Job->>DB: Set job complete with storage_path
            DB-->>Page: Realtime update (PdfJobWatcher)
            Page->>Api: GET /api/pdf/status/{jobId}
            Api->>Api: Check job belongs to caller (proposed)
            Api-->>Page: Presigned download URL
            Page-->>Steward: Download PDF with same answers<br/>and photos as SIR page (AT 1, AT 3)
        end
    end

    Note over Page,Job: includeImages is false by default today.<br/>AT 3 needs photos, so the request must set it.<br/>Today /api/pdf/route.ts does not read the owner. It checks only user_metadata.role === 'admin'.
